<title>USA: Chrysler to operate six of nine U.S. plants.</title>
<headline>Chrysler to operate six of nine U.S. plants.</headline>
<dateline>AUBURN HILLS, Mich. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler said six of its nine U.S. assembly plants and all three Canadian assembly plants will operate the week of January 13.</p>
<p>It said a shutdown at its Belvidere, Ill. plant will be extended by another week. The facility, used to assemble Neons, was shut down this week for inventory adjustment. Chrysler said it has a 99-day supply of Neons.</p>
<p>Chrysler's Conner Avenue (Michigan) and Newark (Delaware) plants will not operate due to model changeover.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
